      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-325470",
      ":question/problem": "The frequency table below shows the number of values in a dataset that fall into each group.\nRounded to one decimal place, what is the largest possible value of the mean?\n\n| Value $(x)$ | Frequency $(f)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $30 - 32$ | $3$ |\n| $32 - 34$ | $4$ |\n| $34 - 36$ | $2$ |\n| $36 - 38$ | $5$ |\n| $38 - 40$ | $1$ |\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
